<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bonn Agreement (2001)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2001">2001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Bonn Conference 2001 · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-in-afghanistan-2001-2021">War in Afghanistan (2001–2021)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a> Agreement was signed on 5 December 2001 in Bonn, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, by Afghan factions opposed to the Taliban under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> auspices. It set up an Afghan Interim Authority led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamid-karzai">Hamid Karzai</a>, provided for a loya jirga to choose a transitional government and a new constitution, and requested an international security force for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>. It laid the basis of the Islamic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>.</p></div>
